  "query_preview": "..\n\nA shortwave trough will exit the Pacific Northwest and dig over \neastern Montana this morning. Ample moisture associated with the \ntrough will result in increased cloud cover and low chances (25%) \nfor scattered showers across northeast Montana today. \n\nRainfall totals are not anticipated to exceed 0.01\" south of \nHighway 2. North of the highway, rainfall totals have a 15-30% \nchance of exceeding 0.01\", with higher chances concentrated \neastward. Locations east of Plentywood have a 15% chance of \nreceiving up to 0.05\" of rainfall.\n\nThe shortwave trough will exit eastward ahead of an upper-level\nridge that will build over Montana tonight. The ridge will persist\nthrough the end of the work week, resulting in temperatures above\nseasonal averages and predominantly dry conditions through Friday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Increased PoPs slightly above initial NBM guidance. \n\n- Confidence in widespread low rain totals is high (80%).\n  Confidence in localized higher amounts is lower (30%).\n\n\nDON",
